  "privacyHeading": "What this app does with your data",
  "privacyOnDeviceTitle": "Everything stays on this phone",
  "privacyOnDeviceBody": "This app has no internet permission. It is removed from the app's manifest, and an automated check on every release refuses to build an app that asks for it. There is no account, no sync, no analytics and no crash reporting. Nothing you record can leave this device unless you export it yourself.",
  "privacyNotEncryptedTitle": "The database is not encrypted",
  "privacyNotEncryptedBody": "This is the honest limit of what \"private\" means here. Your data sits in this app's own storage, which other apps cannot read on a phone that has not been tampered with, and which Android's full-device encryption protects while the phone is switched off. But it is stored as plain text. Anyone who picks up your unlocked phone, or who takes a forensic copy of it, can read it. There is no app lock in this version.",
  "privacyBackupTitle": "It is never backed up to the cloud",
  "privacyBackupBody": "Android's automatic backup is switched off for this app, so your cycle history is never copied to a Google account. The consequence is that if you lose the phone, the data is gone unless you exported it.",
  "privacyDeletionTitle": "Deleting really deletes",
  "privacyDeletionBody": "Deleting a day removes the row. Deleting everything removes every row and then reclaims the space, so the old entries are not left readable in the file. Nothing is kept behind a hidden flag.",
  "privacyLogsTitle": "The activity log holds no cycle content",
